WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:07.330
Vibration builds during steady flight and is
also observed on the ground. This uses

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:14.631
synthetic data and a preselected operator
measurement plan, executed with local Qwen3

00:00:14.631 --> 00:00:15.490
Coder 30B.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:22.570
RAG retrieves relevant setup and quality
passages with their source IDs and revisions.

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:28.318
Bearing geometry is verified against the
document for the same machine and

00:00:28.318 --> 00:00:35.231
configuration. Retrieved text is reference
context; the recordings supply the measurement

00:00:35.231 --> 00:00:35.930
evidence.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:43.810
The workflow reviews data quality and
separates the physical vibration monitor from

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:51.561
the alarm flag. Flight and ground recordings
retain independent source identities. The

00:00:51.561 --> 00:00:58.320
original inputs are preserved; native C++
tools calculate the measurements.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:08.340
Early and late flight windows compare speed,
torque and vibration. FFT and measured-encoder

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:17.854
order analysis test rotational explanations.
The ground check is a separate recording, not

00:01:17.854 --> 00:01:20.920
another window of the flight.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:28.282
Bearing signatures are tested separately on
both sensors in flight and ground recordings.

00:01:28.282 --> 00:01:35.323
A single large FFT peak is insufficient: the
family and harmonics must agree with measured

00:01:35.323 --> 00:01:42.520
speed and documented geometry, and independent
evidence must test installation alternatives.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:49.642
Both sensors in both recordings support the
approximately 107.4 Hz outer-race signature,

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:55.601
weakening a single-sensor installation-only
explanation. The Agent revises its

00:01:55.601 --> 00:02:01.941
evidence-linked assessment after operator
report review. Physical damage and repair

00:02:01.941 --> 00:02:05.990
effectiveness still require independent
confirmation.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:13.641
Finally, a quick look at the latest report
from this run: actual computed plots,

00:02:13.641 --> 00:02:21.164
numerical tables, cited sources and the
assessment. These are pages of the exported

00:02:21.164 --> 00:02:26.240
PDF, available through the report link beside
the video.
